cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "dpd-stream"
abstract: "Out-of-core difference and system GMM for dynamic panels (Arellano-Bond, Blundell-Bond). One-step, two-step or iterated estimation with flexible instrument sets, Windmeijer-corrected and clustered inference, specification and identification tests, Ahn-Schmidt nonlinear moments and absorbed fixed effects, computed in streamed passes so that panel data far larger than memory can be used. Conventions follow Stata's xtabond2; results are tested against it, xtdpdgmm and other implementations."
authors:
  - family-names: Tucker
    given-names: Lee
    email: lee.c.tucker@census.gov
version: 0.2.0
date-released: 2026-10-31
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/leetucker/dpd-stream"
url: "https://github.com/leetucker/dpd-stream"
keywords:
  - econometrics
  - dynamic panel data
  - GMM
  - Arellano-Bond
  - Blundell-Bond
  - out-of-core
